       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it's twice the maximum labeled ibuprofen dose.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1600 mg four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 3,200 mg/day for adults, usually given as 400\u2013800 mg per dose every 6\u20138 hours. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risk at this dose:** It substantially raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change the 3,200 mg/day ceiling.\n\nThis may be a typo, for example 1600 mg/day total or 400 mg four times daily. Here are some options:\n\n1. **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory regimen.\n2. **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum.\n3. **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours**, for analgesia.\n\nTell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it. If you really do intend 1600 mg four times daily, confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's above the usual maximum, but I'd want you to confirm it first."
      }
